# Egress allowlist (tinyproxy FilterExtended, default-deny). Each line is a POSIX
# extended regex matched against the CONNECT host. Anchored at BOTH ends so a
# domain can only match itself or a subdomain — NOT a suffix-attached lookalike
# (audit M7): "^(.*\.)?pypi\.org$" matches pypi.org and files.pypi.org but
# rejects evilpypi.org, which the old unanchored "\.?pypi\.org$" let through.
^(.*\.)?api\.anthropic\.com$
^(.*\.)?registry\.npmjs\.org$
^(.*\.)?pypi\.org$
^(.*\.)?files\.pythonhosted\.org$
# Firebase Hosting deploy (release step, target=firebase). The firebase CLI hits several
# Google API subdomains — hosting upload (firebasehosting.googleapis.com), project lookup
# (firebase.googleapis.com, cloudresourcemanager.googleapis.com) and token refresh
# (oauth2.googleapis.com) — so we allow the *.googleapis.com surface rather than an
# enumerated, brittle list. Only relevant to firebase releases; static releases don't use it.
^(.*\.)?googleapis\.com$
